From 0647a2fd75b988cf38aac30c30c6cb407fcccb6e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lancethepants <lancethepants@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 14:46:30 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Support Wi-Fi 6 mt76 radios (mt7915) with --any-driver

The dashboard works on other mt76 chips: iw, nl80211, the survey and
hostapd are driver-neutral, and mt7915 has the same debugfs files with
a tx_stats header the parser already accepts. Tested on a GL-MT6000
(MT7986, mt7915 driver as mt798x-wmac, with guest, IoT and mesh
interfaces next to the main APs):

- Puncturing advice was given for any 80+ MHz channel, but preamble
  puncturing of the BSS is a Wi-Fi 7 (EHT) feature. Read ieee80211be
  from hostapd status and give no puncturing advice on a BSS that is
  not EHT (unknown, without hostapd status: as before).
- Kernel log lines of the mt7915 driver (mt7915e, or mt798x-wmac on the
  MT7981/MT7986 built-in radios) were not followed.
- The Links column of a client without per-link data was empty ('-');
  show the band of its interface when that is unambiguous.
- Every interface got its own plan, so a radio with guest/IoT/mesh BSSes
  was planned several times, and a mesh point reporting 20 MHz next to
  40 MHz APs got contradictory advice. Plan each radio (or MLO link)
  once, from the AP interface with the most clients.
- 2.4 GHz channel advice is only computed for 20 MHz; say so in a plan
  note instead of showing an empty candidate list.
---
